  "releaseNotes": "📦 Release Notes – Version 1.0.5\n✨ New Features\nMulti-State Configuration Support\n\nIntroduced .ForStates method in DStateMachine, allowing configuration to be applied to multiple states simultaneously.\n\nAdded MultiStateConfiguration class enabling unified configuration of:\n\nEntry and exit actions\n\nTrigger transitions\n\nThis significantly simplifies the setup of shared behavior across multiple states without sacrificing full control.\n\n🧪 Tests\nAdded unit tests to ensure transitions work correctly when configured using .ForStates.\n\n📚 Documentation\nUpdated the README:\n\nAdded usage example for .ForStates\n\nIncluded in the “Getting Started” section to help users quickly adopt the new approach.\n\n✅ Summary\nThese enhancements streamline state machine configuration, reduce duplication, and provide a clean way to manage shared behaviors across states—improving maintainability and developer productivity.",
